  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "A solid box is \\(15\\) cm by \\(10\\) cm by \\(8\\) cm. A new solid is formed by removing a cube \\(3\\) cm on a side from each corner of this box. What percent of the original volume is removed?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(4.5\\)",
    "B": "\\(9\\)",
    "C": "\\(12\\)",
    "D": "\\(18\\)",
    "E": "\\(24\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "We need the removed volume as a fraction of the original volume. The original box has volume\n\\[\n15\\cdot10\\cdot8=1200\\text{ cm}^3.\n\\]\nA box has eight corners. Since every box dimension exceeds \\(2\\cdot3=6\\) cm, the cubes cut from different corners do not overlap. Each cube has volume \\(3\\cdot3\\cdot3=27\\text{ cm}^3\\), so the total volume removed is \\(8\\cdot27=216\\text{ cm}^3\\).\n\nThe fraction removed is\n\\[\n\\frac{216}{1200}=\\frac{18}{100}=18\\%.\n\\]\nThus \\(\\boxed{18\\%}\\) of the original volume is removed, choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
